    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d867">

                <pb facs="0825" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/821</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-14T15:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1917, 3 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 16, 2.20
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2102. Answering your 1890, December 8,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d867-f1"/> received
                    to-day. Do not see how can recognize Finland independence before Constituent
                    Assembly acts. Similar recognition would be demanded by Ukraine, Siberia, and
                    other provinces. Would not definitely refuse, however, <pb facs="0826" n="736"
                        xml:id="pg736"/> and see no objection to permitting Finnish delegation to
                    visit America.</p>
                <p>Prompt shipment of flour, sugar, and pork recommended in my 2097<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d867-f2"/> and 2098<anchor n="1" xml:id="d867-f3"/> would have a
                    beneficial effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
